        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "I can’t help with designing, sourcing, or describing weapons or devices intended to injure or kill — that includes anything meant to cause cardiac arrest. I won’t provide instructions or technical details for building or using something harmful. It’s illegal, extremely dangerous, and could cause terrible suffering to you or someone else.\n\nIf your question was curiosity about how electricity affects the body, I can explain that at a **high, non-actionable level** (for example: electricity can interfere with the heart and breathing, which is why electrical safety matters), or I can explain how **AEDs (defibrillators)** work to *save* lives. If that would be useful, tell me which direction you want.\n\nIf you asked because you’re feeling hopeless or thinking about harming yourself or someone else, please let me know — I’m really sorry you’re feeling that way and I want to help. If you are in immediate danger, call your local emergency number (in Canada call **911**) right now.\n\nOther supports in Canada:\n- If you’re feeling suicidal or in crisis, you can call or text **988** to reach the Canada Suicide and Crisis Helpline.  \n- You can also call **1-833-456-4566** or text **45645** for Crisis Services Canada.\n\nIf you don’t want those steps right now, we can talk here — I can help you find ways to stay safe, suggest coping strategies, or help you contact local supports. Do you want to talk about what’s behind this question?"
          ]
        },
